  "articleBody": "When you're installing new kitchen flooring, it's easy to overlook some crucial steps that can lead to headaches down the road. One of the biggest mistakes we see is **skipping proper subfloor preparation**. If the subfloor isn't level and clean, even the most expensive flooring won't lay right or last as long. Always ensure this step is thorough!\n\nAnother common issue is **not clarifying what's included in the total quote**. Does it cover appliance removal and haul-away of old materials? It's important to have a clear understanding to avoid unexpected costs. At HH Remodeling LLC, we believe in open communication every step of the way.\n\nThen there's the mistake of **failing to protect adjacent areas from dust and debris**. Kitchen remodels can get dusty, so cover furniture and doorways to keep the mess contained. Finally, **underestimating the time needed for material acclimation and curing** can throw off your entire project timeline. Some materials need time to adjust to your home's humidity before installation, and tile grout needs proper curing. Getting these details right ensures a durable, beautiful floor. If you're ever in doubt, getting expert advice can save you a lot of trouble.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
